A new NOT NULL column filled from the others in the same migration: no
second deploy, no DEFAULT to invent. Nothing goes, so nothing is copied.
A comment after the expression ends with its line.

== before
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL) STRICT;
INSERT INTO dish VALUES (1, 'Pea Soup'), (2, 'Rye Bread');

== after
-- @release 1
-- @from 1 column dish slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-')) -- for URLs
CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE) STRICT;

== plan
roux: migrating test.db, 4 steps
  table `dish`: aside, to make it anew
    ALTER TABLE "dish" RENAME TO "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: as schema.sql makes it
    CREATE TABLE dish (id INTEGER PRIMARY KEY, name TEXT NOT NULL, slug TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE) STRICT
  table `dish`: its rows, by id, name, slug = lower(replace(name, ' ', '-')) -- for URLs
    INSERT INTO "dish" ("id", "name", "slug") SELECT "id", "name", (
    lower(replace(name, ' ', '-')) -- for URLs
    ) FROM "roux_old_dish"
  table `dish`: the old one
    DROP TABLE "roux_old_dish"
migrated from release 0

== query
SELECT id, name, slug FROM dish ORDER BY id

== rows
1 | Pea Soup | pea-soup
2 | Rye Bread | rye-bread
